[b][color=#3d85c6][size=5]Leveling[/size][/color][/b]

Skill points are earned every time a player levels up, and are divided into five categories: Enforcer, Provisioner, Hustler, Logistician, and Special. 
[b]Every level up[/b]: The player earns a skill point, alternating between the Enforcer, Provisioner, Hustler, Logistician trees, in that order. 
[b]Every rank up[/b]: The player earns a skill point in the Special tree and a bonus skill point in the Enforcer, Provisioner, Hustler, or Logistician tree.

[b]Enforcer[/b]: Grants bonuses to the player's base attributes, such as maximum health, increased XP gain, and movement speed.
[b]Provisioner[/b]: Grants bonuses to crop cultivation and drug production.
[b]Hustler[/b]: Grants bonuses to NPC interactions, player status, and financial transactions.
[b]Logistician[/b]: Grants bonuses to dealers, employees, and suppliers.
[b]Special[/b]: Grants active skills

[size=5][b][color=#3d85c6]Skill Trees[/color][/b][/size]

Most skill parameters are user configurable via [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/schedule1/mods/1222?tab=files]ModsApp[/url] (recommended) and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/schedule1/mods/397]Mod Manager - Phone App[/url], or the [i]SkillTree_Config.cfg[/i] located at [i]Schedule 1\User Data\SkillTree_Config.cfg[/i]. Most settings don't have any limits, aside from the few that are much more likely to break things. Reload the save after making changes for them to apply.

