[color=#3d85c6][size=5][b]For Translators[/b][/size][/color]

The language files are extracted to [i]UserData/SkillTree/Localization[/i] when you load the game, and each locale has its own directory containing JSON files with all the text for notifications, skill names, and skill descriptions.
 
[list=1]
[*]en_US is the only locale at the moment, so make a copy of that directory and its contents
[*]Rename the new directory to whatever you want (the name doesn't matter, but don't put periods '.' in the name)
[*]Some text contains numbers surrounded in curly braces/brackets ({0},{1}, and so on). These are used for inserting values into the text while the game is running. Don't delete these.
[*]Standard JSON formatting rules apply
[/list]
There two language-related options under User Settings: [b]Locale[/b] and [b]Overwrite Locale Files

[/b]Change [b]Locale[/b] to the name of the directory in [i]UserData/SkillTree/Localization[/i] that you want to load, save the setting, and the text will automatically change without having to reload the save. I confirmed that reloading is not needed when using [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/schedule1/mods/1222?tab=files]ModsApp[/url], I didn't test with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/schedule1/mods/397]Mod Manager - Phone App[/url].

[b]Overwrite Locale Files[/b] is the list of locales that will be overwritten with default data when the game loads. Remove locales from the list if you want to customize them. Currently, en_US is the only locale with default data, so this setting only matters if you want to change the default English text. 

[b][color=#3d85c6][size=5]Notes[/size][/color][/b]

[list]
[*][b]Multiplayer[/b]: I haven't tested multiplayer at all. There will be bugs and probably very few fixes for them.
[*][b]Feedback[/b]: If you encounter bugs, have balance suggestions, or new ideas, please notify me on the mod page.
[*][b]Open Source[/b]: SkillTree (Forked) is open source and distributed with the same licenses as the original: non-commercial use only, accepting donations is fine, and you must credit the original authors. Feel free to fork, modify, and learn from it.
[*][b]AI Usage[/b]: The original mod used AI code for the Harmony patches, and I've gutted most of it.
[/list]
